---
import { PREVIEW_PRIVACY_URL } from "@volli/shared";
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
---

<Legal
  title="Preview Agreement"
  description="The agreement for Volli’s free, invite-only 0.3 preview: no SLA, possible data loss, and your responsibilities when using agents."
  path="/legal/preview/"
>
  <p>
    This agreement is between you and Hussain Phalasiya, the operator of Volli in Ontario,
    Canada ("Volli", "we"). It covers the invite-only Volli 0.3 cloud preview. By choosing to
    continue with sign-in after being shown this agreement, you agree to it. If you do not
    agree, do not join the preview. If you join for an organization, you must have its authority.
  </p>

  <h2>A free, unfinished preview</h2>
  <p>
    We do not charge for this preview. There is no paid subscription or automatic conversion
    to one. Your model providers and other services may charge you under your own agreements.
    We may change, suspend or end the preview or your access to it. An invitation is for you;
    do not share sign-in credentials or bypass invitation or security controls.
  </p>
  <p>
    The preview is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties to the extent the
    law allows. There is no service-level agreement (SLA), uptime commitment or guaranteed
    support. Features may break, and data may be lost or reset. Keep independent copies of
    work you cannot lose. Do not rely on the preview for critical or regulated work.
  </p>

  <h2>You direct the agents</h2>
  <p>
    Agents can run commands, change or delete files, and send data to external services using
    the access you give them. They can make mistakes or be misled by content they read.
    Choose their access carefully and review code, commands and other output before relying
    on it. You are responsible for the actions you authorize, the content you submit, and
    compliance with your model providers' terms. Do not use Volli unlawfully, harm others,
    access systems without permission, or interfere with the service's security.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content and cloud history</h2>
  <p>
    You keep your rights in the content you submit. We claim no ownership of your content or
    model output; we assign to you any rights we have in that output. Other people's rights
    and model-provider terms may still apply. You permit us to store, process, transmit and
    display your content only to provide, secure and support the preview and comply with law.
    We do not use it to train AI models.
  </p>
  <p>
    Signed-in Workspace data and Session history sync to our service providers, even when
    tools run on your Mac. History can contain code, command output and secrets. Workspace
    members may see shared work. Read the <a href={PREVIEW_PRIVACY_URL}>Privacy page</a> before
    submitting data. Agreement to these terms is not consent to optional telemetry.
  </p>

  <h2>Stopping and changes</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using the preview at any time. For access, export or deletion requests,
    contact us privately through your preview invitation. We will publish material changes
    with a new agreement version and ask you to accept before continuing under that version.
    These terms do not change the open-source licenses of released Volli code.
  </p>

  <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
  <p>
    Ontario law and applicable Canadian federal law govern this agreement, subject to any
    mandatory protections where you live. Nothing in this agreement excludes rights,
    warranties or liability that the law does not allow us to exclude.
  </p>
</Legal>
